{
    "npc_key": "dorcas_fenn",
    "start": "greeting",
    "nodes": {
        "greeting": [
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "quest": "the_uncounted",
                        "stage": "to_the_record"
                    }
                ],
                "text": "Dorcas Fenn reads Tull's page and the fifteen lines you copied from the day book, and then reads them again with her lips moving, which she does not usually do. \"There is no head for this,\" she says. \"Nobody has ever brought me one. I can enter it as given: a count, by a named party, on these sources.\" She uncaps the ink. \"It won't be a finding. It will be a record. They aren't the same thing, and I'd want you to know that before I write.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Enter it as given.",
                        "effects": [
                            {
                                "quest_stage": {
                                    "quest": "the_uncounted",
                                    "stage": "entered"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
                        "next": "uncounted_entered"
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "Not yet.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "flag": "mearing_recut"
                    },
                    {
                        "flag": "act_two_open"
                    }
                ],
                "once": true,
                "text": "\"A surveyor's sheet came down from your valley,\" Dorcas says, \"an old chainman's hand, with two readings for one stone and a line ruled between them.\" She almost smiles. \"I have filed it under Disputed. It's a shelf nobody likes. Everything on it will be argued about for a hundred years, and at least now the argument is written down.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Leave.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "has_item": "priory_cartulary"
                    },
                    {
                        "flag": "act_two_open"
                    },
                    {
                        "not": {
                            "flag": "cartulary_deposited"
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "text": "Dorcas Fenn sees the binding before she sees you. \"That's a fourth press,\" she says. \"Arden's, by the tooling. A decade of deeds and bounds.\" She does not reach for it. \"A Record Office takes deposits. It would be kept dry, entered, and open to anybody who asks, and it would still be the priory's to ask back. Very little has come to us from up your valley that the house didn't send.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Take it. Enter it as Arden's.",
                        "effects": [
                            {
                                "take_item": "priory_cartulary"
                            },
                            {
                                "set_flag": "cartulary_deposited"
                            },
                            {
                                "approval": {
                                    "aldric": 4,
                                    "sera": -2
                                }
                            }
                        ],
                        "next": "cartulary_entered"
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "I'll keep it.",
                        "effects": [
                            {
                                "set_flag": "cartulary_deposited",
                                "value": "kept"
                            }
                        ],
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "flag": "concern_answering"
                    },
                    {
                        "flag": "uncounted_fate",
                        "equals": "entered"
                    }
                ],
                "once": true,
                "text": "Dorcas Fenn has a letter pinned flat under the ledger weight, and she lets you read the top of it. It asks, with every courtesy, that the entry headed The Deepworks be closed to inspection pending correction. \"I have written back,\" she says. \"A record given is open. It can be amended by the informant and by nobody else, and the informant is you.\" She squares the ledger. \"They will have had the right answer. I don't suppose they will like it, and I don't suppose they will write again. They will do something else.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Leave it exactly as it is.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "flag": "concern_asking"
                    },
                    {
                        "flag": "uncounted_fate",
                        "equals": "entered"
                    }
                ],
                "once": true,
                "text": "\"A gentleman from the house asked to read your Deepworks entry,\" Dorcas says. \"He had every right. He read it twice, made no copy, and asked whether there was a fee for a correction.\" She turns a page. \"There isn't. Not for a record given. I told him who the informant was, because he asked, and because it's written at the top.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Leave.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "flag": "uncounted_fate",
                        "equals": "entered"
                    }
                ],
                "once": true,
                "text": "\"Somebody came in to read your entry,\" Dorcas says. \"A woman from Greyhythe, looking for a name. It wasn't there, or it was and it wasn't his.\" She straightens the ledger. \"She stayed an hour anyway. I didn't hurry her.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Leave.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "quest": "a_record_is_not_the_thing",
                        "stage": "the_field_books"
                    }
                ],
                "text": "\"Rivermark,\" says the woman at the top of the ladder, and comes down it with a stack of narrow, swollen books bound in green cloth. \"Forty-one field books. Chain, angles, levels, the margins.\" She lays them on the long table. \"A penny a page to read, a penny to copy, and nothing leaves the room. You'll have brought a copy of your own. People do.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Lay the survey beside them.",
                        "next": "beside"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "quest": "the_fenmoor_lot",
                        "stage": "lot_forty_one"
                    }
                ],
                "text": "\"The Fenmoor lot,\" Dorcas Fenn says from the ladder. \"Greyhythe returns, four years back.\" The ladder rolls along the rail, three yards, five, and stops. \"Here.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Read the return.",
                        "next": "fenmoor_return"
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "Leave.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "has_item": "fenmoor_crate_lid"
                    },
                    {
                        "flag": "armour_chain_ended"
                    }
                ],
                "once": true,
                "text": "Dorcas Fenn comes all the way down the ladder for the lid, which she does not do for most things. \"Lot forty-one,\" she says. \"That's the Greyhythe sale's stencil. That's the return I showed you, and that's Darrow's sale at the Weir, and that's Abe Treen's chalk.\" She goes back up for the return and writes in the margin, very small: lid seen. \"The chain is whole,\" she says from the top. \"It has a hole in the middle where a name would go, and the hole is whole as well. I'll file it that way.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Leave.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "flag": "survey_fate",
                        "equals": "warned"
                    }
                ],
                "once": true,
                "text": "\"You're from up the valley,\" Dorcas Fenn says, without looking round from the shelf. \"We've had three conveyances in from Granary Row this fortnight. People sell quicker once they know. I don't think that's anybody's fault. I just thought somebody from there ought to be told it was filed.\"",
